    {
      "id": "_lC-y2z5BgeVqCWnS4hpx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 271.3965756520806,
      "y": -1259.0945046253564,
      "width": 2020.4206428467892,
      "height": 873.6,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "az",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1974355993,
      "version": 216,
      "versionNonce": 1000202489,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793817250921,
      "created": 1793817215789,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n## Two Problems Hiding As One - they are really the same problem\n\nRight now or Software API is saying it can create a license. It cannot.\n(It can create a vendor, because it owns all the operands)\nOne problem is the call is too slow. Have some standards!\nThe other, though, is that we are gambling on a distributed transaction.\n\nThe only failure that can be handled is the client not knowing if you got the request. Send the first one with an\nIdempotency-Key - store it. Check it when the post comes in again.\n\nBy distributing our app across multiple coupled services we are multiplying the likelihood of a failure. (\"3 always\", load\nbalancing, K8S, etc.)\n\n\n\n1. This is too slow, let's return a guess, and work on it in the background.\n        1. Use a channel\n        2. Use a database, poll.\n        3. \"This API can't keep up with the demand in an appropriate amount of time, so we will make everything worse.\"\n                1. Background work can get backpressure, etc. \n                2. Database polling? (though things like pings from triggers, etc. are a little better)\n2. The Software.Api can't do licensing. \n        - move that to the License.Api?\n        - But the software API *needs* that data!\n                - Share a database? Do a GET frequently? (both may be ok, especially if they are in the same app)",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n## Two Problems Hiding As One - they are really the same problem\n\nRight now or Software API is saying it can create a license. It cannot.\n(It can create a vendor, because it owns all the operands)\nOne problem is the call is too slow. Have some standards!\nThe other, though, is that we are gambling on a distributed transaction.\n\nThe only failure that can be handled is the client not knowing if you got the request. Send the first one with an Idempotency-Key - store it. Check it when the post comes in again.\n\nBy distributing our app across multiple coupled services we are multiplying the likelihood of a failure. (\"3 always\", load balancing, K8S, etc.)\n\n\n\n1. This is too slow, let's return a guess, and work on it in the background.\n        1. Use a channel\n        2. Use a database, poll.\n        3. \"This API can't keep up with the demand in an appropriate amount of time, so we will make everything worse.\"\n                1. Background work can get backpressure, etc. \n                2. Database polling? (though things like pings from triggers, etc. are a little better)\n2. The Software.Api can't do licensing. \n        - move that to the License.Api?\n        - But the software API *needs* that data!\n                - Share a database? Do a GET frequently? (both may be ok, especially if they are in the same app)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
